! mcp_bootstrap_p163.strap -- the SPACE BLOCK, SPACE FILE, K FIL K1 and
! K N SYST paths of the tape-command interpreter, printed page 163.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.170.  The header was READ and not
! assumed: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID IH000042   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  163", and the
! column-heading row's own LOCATION field reads 220147, which is line
! 1's word (rendered on its own at 900 dpi -- the digits are there, it
! is not the dashed rule).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FORTY-SIX PRINTED LINES, EVERY ONE OF WHICH EMITS BITS.  There is no
! SLC, no DD, no SYN, no reservation and no banner: forty-six
! consecutive instructions, 220147.40 through 220202.40, with NO HOLE
! anywhere in the span.  Both CNOPs (lines 3 and 21) found the counter
! on a HALF word and so each emitted a real half-word no-op
! "000000.30 00" at its own printed location -- unlike printed p.156
! line 11, whose CNOP was already aligned and printed neither a
! location nor any bits.
!
! THE SURVEY SAID 33 ROWS AND IT WAS COUNTING CARDS, NOT LINES.  The
! card-serial column runs IH000042 .. IH000074 -- thirty-three
! serials, contiguous, no gap -- and thirteen of them carry TWO
! printed statements (the SIC/branch pairs and the LX/SX pairs), which
! is exactly 33 + 13 = 46.  Nothing fell off either end: serial
! IH000042 is also the CARD ID in the page header, and the last line
! is IH000074.
!
! The page is four fragments back to back:
!
!   lines 1-12   the tail of the SPACE BLOCK command begun on printed
!                p.162: save the IC in K K IND / go to K IO IND, then
!                CNOP, build the I/O instruction in place (LX/SX
!                through S IO INS), the CTL with the decimal command
!                62, set the SET UP bit under K SUPP, offer it, and
!                leave through M IO REJ or through E IND R / E IO IND.
!   lines 13-18  K SP TM, "SPACE OVER TAPE MARK": pull the two-bit
!                density out of S F DEN, skip the alternative with
!                BRN, else take the label density out of S LABD, put
!                the return address in $R and call K DENST.
!   lines 19-30  the SPACE FILE command, line for line the same shape
!                as lines 1-12 with the octal command (8)77 in place
!                of the decimal 62.
!   lines 31-35  K FIL K1: set the file count to +1 (S FILEK), pick up
!                the return address out of S SCRPM, clear the CTL bit
!                with CM0000, and return through B,0.0($1).
!   lines 36-46  K N SYST ("new system"): the same file-count bump,
!                then S F DEN / BRN / LI(BU,1),S TD DEN -- i.e. the
!                STANDARD DENSITY literal instead of a loaded field --
!                and out through K DENST and K IO IND to Z STEVL.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHERE THE PAGE JOINS, AND IT JOINS AT BOTH ENDS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The page prints no SLC, so its origin is the counter arriving from
! printed p.162 and the deck ASSERTS it with a hard SLC (which cannot
! disagree with a counter it overrides -- see
! docs/transcription_workflow.md, "A HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE").  Two
! readings INDEPENDENT of this page's LOCATION column agree on
! 220147.40:
!
!   * the column-heading row's own LOCATION field reads 220147; and
!   * docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt line 8397 is printed p.162's OWN
!     last row -- a DIFFERENT page, so a real witness --
!     "46* 220147.00  217674.50 00  B,K DENST  -SET UNIT TO
!     INSTALAATICN DEN", a half-word branch at 220147.00 which leaves
!     the counter at exactly 220147.40.
!
! THE FAR END IS WITNESSED TOO.  Line 46 is a half word at 220202.40,
! so the counter leaves this page at 220203.00; the volume OCR of
! printed p.164 (PDF p.171, a DIFFERENT page) opens with a three-line
! asterisk banner "*** WRITE END OF FILE ***" and its first located
! row is line 4 at "220203.00 *".  So printed p.164's FIRST LOCATION
! IS 220203.00 and that is corroborated, not predicted.  TWO ACTUAL
! PREDICTIONS for its transcriber, neither of them read: its first
! card serial is IH000075, and its heading LOCATION field is BLANK,
! because its line 1 is a banner that compiles nothing (the rule
! measured over sixteen pages in docs/transcription_workflow.md).
!
! TWO OF THIS PAGE'S OWN LABELS ARE PINNED BY printed p.162, not by
! this page's ink:
!   * OCR line 8396, p.162 line 45: "BZB,$5.224,K SP TM" against
!     220156.74 -- 0o74 = K SP TM's own .40 plus BZB's .34 -- i.e.
!     K SP TM = 220156.40, this page's line 13.
!   * OCR line 8394, p.162 line 43: "RS1 FLK  BZB,S SYSTM($12),K N
!     SYST" against 220174.74, i.e. K N SYST = 220174.40, this page's
!     line 36.
! K FIL K1 is referenced from a later page (OCR line 9690,
! "221372.00  220171.45 04 ... K FIL K?"), whose 220171.45 is this
! page's line 31 at 220171.40 plus .05 of operation bits; that
! reference corroborates the ADDRESS but its OCR of the NAME is
! garbled, so the spelling rests on this page's ink (read at 900 dpi:
! K, space, F I L, space, K 1 -- eight characters, which is the full
! width of the NAME field).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! NO SUBSTITUTIONS.  EVERY ROW IS THE PRINTED CARD.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Forty-six printed statements were handed to strap_asm exactly as
! printed and all forty-six compiled to the printed bits on the first
! try.  Nothing is left failing, nothing is labelled, nothing was
! dropped.  In particular:
!
! * LINE 24'S DOTTED OCTAL CONTROL CODE NOW COMPILES.  The page prints
!   "CTL,0.0($14),(8)77." and strap_asm renders "000000.00 8E
!   000077.05 00", which is the printed pair.  This is the exact form
!   printed p.156 line 14 had to leave FAILING ("(8)117." compiled to
!   011700.05 00, the octal shifted six bits left).  The word-granular
!   fix landed since.  MEASURED, not suggested: "cd tests &&
!   PYTHONPATH=../strap python3 verify_mcp_page.py 156" now prints
!   "PASS MCP p.156 217753.00 line 14 CTL,0.0($14),(8)117. ...
!   assembled '000000.00 8E 000117.05 00'" and "ALL TESTS PASSED" for
!   all 27 of its rows.  So p.156's PROSE IS NOW STALE: it still says
!   that row is "LEFT FAILING ON PURPOSE" and that its statement and
!   its !CHECK contradict each other, and they no longer do.  Fixing
!   that comment is outside this page's scope and is flagged here.
! * LINE 6'S DECIMAL CONTROL CODE AGREES WITH IT.  "CTL,0.0($14),62."
!   renders "000076.05 00"; 62 decimal is 0o76, which is what the page
!   prints, so the decimal and the octal spellings of the same field
!   are both right on one page.
! * LINE 40 IS AN IMMEDIATE, AND ITS DATUM IS WITNESSED TO ONE BIT --
!   WHICH IS A SIXTH ENTRY FOR "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE".
!   "LI(BU,1),S TD DEN,46" renders "000000.00 80 401027.20 50", the
!   printed pair.  An LI's first half word holds the DATUM and not an
!   address, and a short field is LEFT-justified in the 24-bit A24
!   field (Reference Manual p.56 "Field Definition", quoted at
!   strap/strap_asm.py:311-324), so a ONE-BIT immediate puts the
!   value's low bit at A24's bit 0 and discards everything else.
!   MEASURED, varying nothing but the SYN and assembling
!   "LI(BU,1),X,46":
!
!       X = 0     -> 000000.00 80 401027.20 50
!       X = 1.0   -> 000000.00 80 401027.20 50
!       X = 0.32  -> 000000.00 80 401027.20 50
!       X = 2.0   -> 000000.00 80 401027.20 50
!       X = 8     -> 000000.00 80 401027.20 50
!       X = 1     -> 400000.00 80 401027.20 50
!
!   So this row establishes only that S TD DEN's value is EVEN.  That
!   it is 0 comes from printed p.108 line 8's DEFINING card, a
!   different page, and not from here.  An earlier draft of this deck
!   said the row "pins S TD DEN's value to 0 exactly"; it does not,
!   and the measurement above is why the sentence was removed.
!   The leading 4 of the second half word, against line 15's
!   "001027.20 50" for the same dds and offset, is the P
!   (addressing-mode) field: P=4 is Immediate addressing, Reference
!   Manual Appendix A footnote 3 ("This operation code may be
!   suffixed by the letter 'I' to invoke immediate addressing"), as
!   quoted at strap/strap_asm.py:126 and :1355-1367.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE INK SAID AND WHAT SETTLED IT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! * THIS DRUM OPENS ROUND GLYPHS CONSTANTLY, AND THE OCTAL FIELDS
!   PROVE IT ROW BY ROW.  Line 5 prints "C0CC04.C1 1C", line 13
!   "C00002.33 8D", line 32 "C0CC07.41 3C", line 35 "C0CC00.1C C1".
!   Every one of those C's sits in a field that can hold only 0-7, so
!   each is a damaged 0 with certainty.
! * BUT A C IN THE HEX BYTE IS USUALLY REAL ON THIS PAGE, and the
!   assembler says which: 1C (lines 5, 23 -- SX with index $12 = C),
!   3C (lines 32, 33, 37 -- SV/LV with $12), 8C (the SICs), C2 (lines
!   14, 39 -- BRN) are all genuine.  The one place the open glyph IS a
!   zero in the byte position is line 35, where "C0CC00.1C C1" is
!   000000.10 01: the trailing byte is 01, the index $1.
! * LINE 40'S SYMBOL IS "S TD DEN", NOT "S IO DEN".  At 400 dpi the
!   two glyphs after the S read I and O.  At 900 dpi the first has a
!   full top bar (T, not I) and the second a straight vertical left
!   stem with squared corners (D, not O or C).  THE INDEPENDENT CHECK
!   IS DECISIVE: printed p.108 line 8 defines "S TD DEN SYN(BU,1),0 --
!   STANDARD DENSITY * 1-LOW, 0-HIGH" at 000000.00, and this page's
!   printed 000000.00 is consistent with it (see the caveat above --
!   the row witnesses only that the value is even).  Of the DEN-suffixed
!   symbols carried by the 148 landed mcp_bootstrap decks' !SYM lines --
!   S F DEN,
!   S U DENS, S TD DEN, T DEN MD, K DENST, K DENOP, K KF DEN, Z CH DEN
!   -- S TD DEN is the only one whose value is 0 (printed p.108 line 6's
!   S INSTD, "INSTALLATION DENSITY", is also 000000.00 but is SYN(BU,24)
!   and is not "S ?? DEN" shaped); that is a measurement
!   over decks/, NOT over the volume, and a page nobody has opened could
!   define another.  (The volume OCR of THIS page reads "DS TO DEND4SE"
!   and is worthless here, as rule 5 says it must be.)
! * CM0000 vs CM0C00 IS NOT A QUESTION.  A connective's mask digits
!   can only be 0 or 1, so line 34's four round glyphs are zeros by
!   construction -- and the second half word confirms it: CM0000
!   prints "001000.00 F0" where line 8's and 26's CM1111 print
!   "001000.36 F0".
! * "IO IND" IS AN O, SETTLED BY RUNG 4 OF THE LADDER ON THIS PAGE
!   ALONE.  The card "B,? IO IND" prints five times here (lines 2, 12,
!   20, 30, 45).  Rendered side by side at 1200 dpi, line 20 prints a
!   FULLY CLOSED O in the same character position where lines 2 and 12
!   print an open C-shaped glyph -- one page, one drum, one card text,
!   one character position, varying only the ink.  The comment column
!   agrees (printed p.156 line 4 reads "-CHECK IO INDS") and so does
!   the English: these are the I/O INDicators.
!
!   THIS CONTRADICTS A LANDED DECK, which is worth the caller's
!   minute: decks/mcp_bootstrap_p160.strap SYNs the same word as
!   EICIND where printed pp.156 and 163 both read E IO IND, and
!   tests/check_symbol_spellings.py already reports it ("two spellings
!   of one symbol at (8)221370.0: EICIND (pp.160) vs EIOIND
!   (pp.156,163) -- glyph C/O").  That hit is PRE-EXISTING -- it fires
!   with this deck removed, with pp.160 and 156 alone -- and this page
!   only adds a third vote on the O side.  Nothing in this deck fixes
!   p.160; saying which reading is right is as far as one page's ink
!   can go.
! * "K DENST" IS D, NOT C: the left stem is straight with squared
!   corners at 900 dpi, and the symbol is pinned anyway by printed
!   p.154's and p.156's decks at (8)217674.40, which is what lines 18
!   and 43 print as "217674.50 00" (.40 plus B's .10).
! * THE SAME-CARD-TWICE ARGUMENT IS AVAILABLE ALL OVER THIS PAGE AND
!   WAS USED: "SIC,K K IND" prints on lines 1, 19, 29 and 44,
!   "B,K IO IND" on 2, 20, 30 and 45, "SX,0,S IO INS($12)" on 5 and
!   23, "L(B,2,1),S F DEN($13),46" on 13 and 38, "BRN,$+1.32" on 14
!   and 39.  Every repetition compiles the same word and every one is
!   checked below, so a misread glyph in any of them would have had to
!   be misread identically four times.
! * ONE PRINTED DIFFERENCE IS REAL AND IS KEPT: line 31 prints
!   "LVI,0,1." and line 36 prints "LVI,0,1.0".  They compile to the
!   same "000001.01 01"; the deck writes each as its own card prints
!   it rather than normalising them.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXACTLY TWO rows carry the extra asterisk after the location:
! line 19 (220162.40 *) and line 38 (220175.40 *).  The whole column
! was rendered on its own, full height, at 600 dpi to be sure there
! are no others, and no row carries the SECOND line-column asterisk
! that printed p.156 line 28 has.
!
! THIS PAGE REFUTES A STATEMENT-KEYED RULE AGAIN, twice over:
! "SIC,K K IND" prints on lines 1, 19, 29 and 44 and only 19 is
! starred; "L(B,2,1),S F DEN($13),46" prints on lines 13 and 38 and
! only 38 is starred.  Same card text, same bits, same index, one
! star.
!
! A PERIODICITY HYPOTHESIS WAS FORMED HERE AND KILLED HERE, so that
! nobody spends an afternoon on it: this page's stars are 19 lines
! apart, and so are printed p.156's (7, 26) and printed p.160's
! (7, 26).  Measured over every landed deck's listing block, the gaps
! are 3, 6, 23 on printed p.112 and 3, 23, 23 on p.111, so there is
! NO periodicity.  The one-liner that measures it:
!   awk '/^! *line +[0-9]+\*?\*? *[0-7]{6}\.[0-7]{2} *\*/ {print FILENAME, $0}' decks/mcp_bootstrap_p1*.strap
! Record it and move on.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT RESTS ON INK ALONE, AND WHAT IS UNOBSERVABLE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! * K FIL K1's SPELLING rests on this page's ink (see above); its
!   ADDRESS does not.
! * Every external SYNed below as "(8)nnnnnn.0" is back-derived from a
!   printed branch, so its bit offset WITHIN the half word is
!   unobservable; the half word itself IS checked.  The SIC rows
!   (1, 19, 29, 44) print the bare 24-bit address, so K K IND IS
!   pinned to the bit at 221371.00; E IND R likewise at 221371.00 from
!   line 11.  K K IND and E IND R are therefore the SAME WORD under
!   two names, and so are K IO IND and E IO IND -- which is exactly
!   what printed p.156 found, independently, on its own lines 3/9 and
!   4/10.
! * S FILEK's bit offset is unobservable from this page: an index-
!   arithmetic operand keeps only bit 32, so lines 32 and 37 would
!   print "000007.41 3C" for 7.38 or for 7.32 alike.  The 7.38 below
!   is printed p.101 line 25's defining card, not a reading of this
!   page.  The same applies to S RET AD, S IO INS and S SCRPM, whose
!   LENGTHS come from p.101 and not from here.
! * S TD DEN, S F DEN, S SET UP, S CTL, S LABD: the dds on each SYN
!   below is the DEFINING page's, carried verbatim so the merged image
!   does not see two pages disagree about one symbol's length.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

SRETAD  SYN(BU,19), 5.0              ! p.101 line 18 -RETURN ADDRESS IN MCP
SIOINS  SYN(BU,64), 4.0              ! p.101 line 17 -IO INSTR. LAST
SSCRPM  SYN(BU,64), 6.0              ! p.101 line 20 -SCRATCH PAD MEMORY
SLABD   SYN(BU,1), 7.29              ! p.101 line 24 -DENSITY SPECIFIED IN
SFILEK  SYN(BU,12), 7.38             ! p.101 line 25 -FILE COUNT
SSETUP  SYN(BU,1), 0.31              ! p.99  line 29 -PSEUDO-OP SET-UP
SCTL    SYN(BU,1), 0.60              ! p.99  line 48 -CONTROL - OPERATION
SFDEN   SYN(BU,2), 2.27              ! p.102 line 12 -IOD DENSITY
STDDEN  SYN(BU,1), 0                 ! p.108 line  8 -STANDARD DENSITY *1-LOW, 0-HIGH
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0             ! as twenty-one other decks write it
MIOREJ  SYN, (8)221261.0             ! off lines 10 and 28; bit offset unobservable
EINDR   SYN, (8)221371.0             ! off the SIC on line 11 -- pinned to the bit
EIOIND  SYN, (8)221370.0             ! off line 12; bit offset unobservable
KKIND   SYN, (8)221371.0             ! off the SICs on 1, 19, 29, 44 -- same word as E IND R
KIOIND  SYN, (8)221370.0             ! off lines 2, 20, 30, 45 -- same word as E IO IND
KDENST  SYN, (8)217674.40            ! off lines 18 and 43; the .40 half word IS checked
ZSTEVL  SYN, (8)221144.40            ! as printed pp.151, 152 and 156 write it

        SLC, (8)220147.40            ! the page prints no SLC; heading LOCATION 220147,
                                     ! and p.162's own line 46 ends at 220147.40

        SIC,KKIND                    ! line  1
        B,KIOIND                     ! line  2  (same card as 1)
        CNOP                         ! line  3  emits a half word: the counter was at .40
        LX,0,$+1.0                   ! line  4
        SX,0,SIOINS($12)             ! line  5  (same card as 4)
        CTL,0.0($14),62.             ! line  6  -SPACE BLOCK COMMAND
        LVI,1,KSUPP                  ! line  7
        CM1111(BU,1),SSETUP($11)     ! line  8
        SIC,SRETAD($12)              ! line  9
        B,MIOREJ                     ! line 10  (same card as 9)
        SIC,EINDR                    ! line 11
        B,EIOIND                     ! line 12  (same card as 11)
KSPTM   L(B,2,1),SFDEN($13),46       ! line 13  -SPACE OVER TAPE MARK
        BRN,$+1.32                   ! line 14
        L(BU,1),SLABD($12),46        ! line 15
        LV,0,$R                      ! line 16
        SIC,SRETAD($12)              ! line 17
        B,KDENST                     ! line 18  (same card as 17)
        SIC,KKIND                    ! line 19  (location carries the trailing asterisk)
        B,KIOIND                     ! line 20  (same card as 19)
        CNOP                         ! line 21  emits a half word: the counter was at .40
        LX,0,$+1.0                   ! line 22
        SX,0,SIOINS($12)             ! line 23  (same card as 22)
        CTL,0.0($14),(8)77.          ! line 24  -SPACE FILE COMMAND
        LVI,1,KSUPP                  ! line 25
        CM1111(BU,1),SSETUP($11)     ! line 26
        SIC,SRETAD($12)              ! line 27
        B,MIOREJ                     ! line 28  (same card as 27)
        SIC,KKIND                    ! line 29
        B,KIOIND                     ! line 30  (same card as 29)
KFILK1  LVI,0,1.                     ! line 31
        SV,0,SFILEK($12)             ! line 32  (same card as 31) -SET FILE COUNT TO +1
        LV,1,SSCRPM($12)             ! line 33  -PICK UP RETURN ADDRESS
        CM0000(BU,1),SCTL($11)       ! line 34
        B,0.0($1)                    ! line 35
KNSYST  LVI,0,1.0                    ! line 36
        SV,0,SFILEK($12)             ! line 37  (same card as 36) -SET FILE COUNT TO +1
        L(B,2,1),SFDEN($13),46       ! line 38  -SET UNIT TO IOD DENSITY
                                     !          (location carries the trailing asterisk)
        BRN,$+1.32                   ! line 39
        LI(BU,1),STDDEN,46           ! line 40
        LV,0,$R                      ! line 41
        SIC,SRETAD($12)              ! line 42
        B,KDENST                     ! line 43  (same card as 42)
        SIC,KKIND                    ! line 44
        B,KIOIND                     ! line 45  (same card as 44)
        B,ZSTEVL                     ! line 46

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, line by line.  The card serial in the right
! margin runs IH000042 .. IH000074 with no gap; it is given for every
! line, because thirteen cards carry two printed lines and the
! repeats are the evidence that 46 lines are 33 cards.
!
!   line  1* 220147.40   221371.00 80                   SIC,K K IND                            IH000042
!   line  2* 220150.00   221370.10 00                   B,K IO IND                             IH000042
!   line  3* 220150.40   000000.30 00                   CNOP                                   IH000043
!   line  4* 220151.00   220152.00 10                   LX,0,$+1.0                             IH000044
!   line  5* 220151.40   000004.01 1C                   SX,0,S IO INS($12)                     IH000044
!   line  6* 220152.00   000000.00 8E 000076.05 00      CTL,0.0($14),62.  -SPACE BLOCK COMMAND IH000045
